x 6.31\\). Therefore, the largest integer \\(k\\) is 6. This means \\(k\\) can be any integer from 1 to 6. Let's list these values:\n\n\\[\nk = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the corresponding cubes:\n\n\\[\n(2 \\cdot 1)^3 = 8, \\quad (2 \\cdot 2)^3 = 64, \\quad (2 \\cdot 3)^3 = 216, \\quad (2 \\cdot 4)^3 = 512, \\quad (2 \\cdot 5)^3 = 1000, \\quad (2 \\cdot 6)^3 = 1728\n\\]\n\nAll of these cubes are less than 2008. Therefore, there are 6 positive even perfect cubes less than 2008.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:62"}
